@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:lightbox-compact a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "A lightbox fits a phone's viewport, its Close button in reach"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/142> , <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/208> ;
    chg:motivation """At phone width the lightbox's panel took its content's minimum width (404 px in a 375 px
viewport), and its header kept the title, the count, Zoom, Open original, the two size toggles and Close in one
row, so Close was past the edge of the screen.""" ;
    chg:substance """Styles only. The lightbox's grid has one minmax(0, 1fr) column and row, and its panel a zero
minimum and a 100 % maximum, so the panel never outgrows the viewport. At compact width the header wraps: the
title and count keep the first row, the actions go to the next, Close at the inline end. Doodle keeps its tilted
panel and, at compact width, leaves room for the tilt (about 1 % of the other dimension). The markup is
unchanged.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing to move. A stylesheet that sized .sem-panel inside a lightbox, or laid out its
.sem-head at compact width, should check it against the new rules.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Nothing to move. Going back, the panel can again be wider than a phone's viewport, and the
header stays one row.""" ;
    chg:affects c:Lightbox .
